iance is concerned that sufficient resources have not been made available to tackle the problem) Tj0.7338 -17.6106  TD 0.0114  Tc 0.5975  Tw (of homelessness, especially at a time when \221care in the community\222 policies are resulting in increas-) Tj-0.2446 -17.8552  TD 0.0088  Tc 0.8991  Tw (ing numbers of people with special needs who require housing.) Tj0 -35.7105  TD 0.0083  Tc 0.4136  Tw (We are concerned about the growth in the number of single persons on the housing waiting list, and) Tj0.4892 -18.0998  TD 0.0304  Tc 0.6789  Tw (feel that there is a need for more accommodation suitable for young persons to be provided both by) Tj0.2446 -17.8552  TD -0.0021  Tc 1.5547  Tw (the Housing Executive and by relevant Housing Associations.) Tj-0.2446 -35.7105  TD 0.0112  Tc 0.8423  Tw (Alliance considers that the current delays in repair and improvement grants are intolerable. These) Tj0.4892 -17.8552  TD 0.0081  Tc 1.8891  Tw (delays have been made worse by recent cuts in government funding. A simple and more flexible) Tj0 -18.0998  TD 0.0246  Tc 1.1276  Tw (grants scheme is needed to speed up applications and approval.) Tj0 -35.7105  TD 0.0032  Tc 0.7376  Tw (Alliance is concerned that improvements in combating urban housing decay have not been matched) Tj0.4892 -17.6106  TD 0.0012  Tc 1.0054  Tw (in the rural housing stock, which now accounts for much of the worst housing conditions in North-) Tj0.2446 -18.0998  TD 0.0214  Tc 0.6332  Tw (ern Ireland. More resources need to be directed towards rural unfitness. Failure to do this can only) Tj0 -18.0998  TD 0.0131  Tc 1.3602  Tw (lead to further rural depopulation and more urban overcrowding.) TjETBT0.9795 0 0 0.9795 36.72 217.2  Tm/F5 12  Tf-0.0592  Tc 0.1534  Tw (14 ) Tj17.8873 0  TD /F2 12  Tf-0.0179  Tc 5.1343  Tw (Alliance Manifesto 1997) TjETendstreamendobj62 0 obj6179endobj60 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 57 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F0 10 0 R /F2 19 0 R /F3 21 0 R /F5 36 0 R >